<p>This is a personal story to me - aside from being a sikh myself, it's a bit of a way to represent my paranoia as it pertains to my anxiety. I feel a lot like Nalwa sometimes. I know other people do too: worrying that they push a lot of people away with their emotions, or that they're a burden, or because they're angry and have huge outbursts. Know that I'm always here for anyone to talk to, yo.</p>
