<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If I had a bit of constructive criticism, I would've maybe made it clear that Mago was lying about the Sikhs against their own desires. I thought Mago was just trying to shield SCP-5550-1 from knowing the unfortunate truth. It never would've occurred to me that Mago didn't write the original containment procedures.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I happened upon this SCP by chance, and it was unexpectedly good. I feel bad for Researcher Mago and SCP-5550-1. Those two were rather cute together, and it's sad to see SCP-5550-1 turn on his friend like that. It was really sweet seeing Mago standing up for Nalwa behind-the-scenese like that.</p>
<p>Overall though, it was a good story. I hope it gets followed up with supplemental tales or something. I really want to know what's become of SCP-5550 now!</p>
<p>Also, more Dr. Trevor Condon Mago pls.</p>

